{"path":"memory/allocator_traits/destroy","title":"std::allocator_traits<Alloc>::destroy","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::allocator_traits&lt;Alloc&gt;::</span>destroy","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits/destroy","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"Calls the destructor of the object pointed to by p. If possible, does so by calling a.destroy(p). If not possible (e.g.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/memory\">&lt;memory&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> destroy<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Alloc<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> a, T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(constexpr since C++20)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Calls the destructor of the object pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code>. If possible, does so by calling <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a.<span class=\"me1\">destroy</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. If not possible (e.g. <code>Alloc</code> does not have the member function <code>destroy()</code>), then calls <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-until-cxx20\"><span>the destructor of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>p</span></code> directly, as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>~T<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></span></span><span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx20\"><span><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/destroy_at\"><span class=\"kw732\">std::<span class=\"me2\">destroy_at</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span></span></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> a\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> allocator to use for destruction\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the object being destroyed\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Because this function provides the automatic fall back to direct call to the destructor, the member function <code>destroy()</code> is an optional <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Allocator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Allocator</em></a> requirement since C++11.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator/destroy\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>destroy</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  destructs an object in allocated storage <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::allocator&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/allocator_traits","title":"std::allocator_traits"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::allocator_traits<Alloc>::destroy","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Calls the destructor of the object pointed to by p. If possible, does so by calling a.destroy(p)."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"a, p"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Because this function provides the automatic fall back to direct call to the destructor, the member function destroy() is an optional Allocator requirement…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"destroy","note":"destructs an object in allocated storage"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":127,"codeBlockCount":0}
